        "kind" : "plus#comment",
        "object" : {
          "content" : "I would question the mounting of the motor on your friend&#39;s machine if it is breaking teeth. It may not be meshing well or is being over-stressed.  <br /><br />With 100% infill the temperature inertia is greater and so warping can be a bigger problem than with lower infill. Though the teeth should be solid fill anyway due to their small area.<br /><br />Good to hear that you solved your problem with the fan settings. -Mike",
          "objectType" : "comment"
        },
